Leads, Contacts, and Accounts

     Understanding the difference between these three "Objects" is the most important part of using Salesforce correctly. Think of it as a funnel:


Object                            What it represents                               The Goal
Lead                              "A ""maybe."" Someone who showed                 Convert them into a 
                                 interest but isn't a customer yet                 Contact/Account once qualified.                                  (e.g., a person who filled out a 
                                 website form)"

Account                          "The Company or organization. This                Track the overall business 
                                 is the ""parent"" record that holds               relationship and history.
                                 everything together."

Contact                          The Individual People who work at                 "Track personal interactions, 
                                 that company. One Account can have                  emails, and meetings."
                                 many Contacts.


       The Conversion Process: In the video, you see a Lead being "Converted." When this happens, Salesforce automatically creates an Account (the company) and a Contact (the person) and optionally an Opportunity (the potential deal).
